  "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/a8c57b12334a23542bae73ba1ac6848e69830b9663a1f83b6340f6812974f416.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2},\\,-2\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{8}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}y\\,\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y\\,{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}y({y}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (0-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
